A||||4||V8Dreamer||I smell oil burning............||||1||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||08-27-2001||12:21 PM||||I have smelled burning oil for the past few days when I get out of my GT after driving a good distance and today when I got to work, I opened the rear deck and noticed an accumulation of oil on top of the tranny housing.  I'm new to the 2.8 and was just wondering if there's a common leak problem that can be easily fixed, if it's probably the head gasket(which I'm fearing it is) or what......I realize that it's hard to tell without looking at it, but I'm just looking for some speculations since I can't look at it myself for at least another 6 hours.<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||08-27-2001||12:33 PM||||Distributor tube O-ring.  Some parts stores carry them, but you may have to go to a dealer.  Still cheap, either way.<P>The original o-ring will harden over time, and not seal worth  crap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Dreamer||08-27-2001||01:17 PM||||Well, good to hear man, thanks a lot.....now that you have mentioned it, that seems like that's exactly where it is coming from.  Any other suggestions from anyone else just incase?<P>TIA,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||08-27-2001||01:28 PM||||the o-ring is a real good bet, check around the valve covers as well. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Dreamer||08-27-2001||01:38 PM||||Cool, I'll do that.  Thanks Larry.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
